Alembic migrations for the Semiconductor Intelligence Platform.

Quickstart
----------
    pip install -e .                     # alembic is a base dependency
    export SEMI_INTEL_DB_URL="sqlite:///./semi_intel.db"   # or a postgres DSN
    alembic upgrade head                 # create/upgrade the schema

After changing a model in semi_intel/domain/models.py:
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"
    # review the generated file in migrations/versions/ before committing --
    # autogenerate is a good first draft, not a guarantee
    alembic upgrade head

Runtime initialization is deliberately not a second schema authority:
`semi-intel init-db` delegates to the same Alembic upgrade path above. Normal
CLI, dashboard, and runtime-bridge sessions then require an exact current
Alembic head before opening a work session. A database created by a bare
`Base.metadata.create_all()` (or with a partial/unknown migration history)
is refused; it is never silently stamped as compatible.

Use `alembic stamp head` only as an explicit, separately reviewed operator
action for a database whose complete schema has already been proven to match
the checked-in migrations. The application never invokes that command as a
fallback.
